---
alwaysApply: true
---

YOU MUST avoid creating large monolith files. If adding new functionality/features to an existing file, you MUST create a new file for the new functionality/features. If you're only updating existing functionality, you may add the edits to the existing file. But in general, prefer encapsulating new functionality/features in a new file to improve readability and maintainability.

When testing locally, you are encouraged to use the `get_local_logs` MCP tool to view the logs of the local services.